{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvRGVzdGlueSUyMCUyODE5OTclMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Destiny","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/pjA38G2fCKTgWsz1HbOcGJalbi1.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cBw8PERRo7wq2zf3WobS1ynDrg3.jpg","description":"In the 12th century's Andalusia lives Ibn Rushd a prominent Islamic philosopher with his wife Zeinab and daughter Salma. The principality is ruled by Khalifa ElMansour who has two sons, ElNasser, an intellectual that likes Ibn Rush and is in love with his daughter Salma. The younger son Abdallah is more into dancing and poetry, spending most of his times with the gypsy family and getting the daughter pregnant. The Khalifa is depending on the extremists to build his army granting them more power which they use to combat artists and philosophers. The extremists succeed in recruiting Abd Allah and train him to kill his father. Events go on where Marawan, the gypsy singer, is killed and Ibn Rushd's books are burnt. Adapted from the real life of Ibn Rushd AlMasir is Chahine's statement against extremism.\n\nReleased 18 Aug 1997 · Egypt, France · Language: Arabic · 129 min\nStudio: Ognon Pictures, MISR International Films, France 2 Cinéma\n\nOn your server — Audio: Arabic · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"1997","genres":["Drama","History","Music","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.8","imdb_id":"tt0119629","moviedb_id":37673,"tmdbId":37673,"runtime":"129 min","cast":["Nour El-Sherif","Hani Salama","Rogena","Layla Olwy","Mahmoud Hemida","Safia ElEmary","Mohamed Mounir","Khaled El Nabawy"],"director":["Youssef Chahine"],"writer":["Youssef Chahine","Khaled Youssef"],"released":"1997-08-18T00:00:00.000Z","country":"Egypt, France","language":"Arabic","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Youssef Chahine","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/eISYmf4YgY39B6ss0jbwwi2gJhz.jpg"},{"name":"Nour El-Sherif","character":"Averroes/Ibn Rushd","p